  "question": {
    ":question/id": "e2200754-27cf-5828-b3a9-2c13fd88937a",
    ":question/problem": "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 3\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $AB.$",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}50 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,50=(-10)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}50 & -30 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-30=(-10)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}50 & -30 \\\\ 10 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,10=(-2)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}50 & -30 \\\\ 10 & -6\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-6=(-2)\\cdot 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}50 & -30 \\\\ 10 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.$",
